From b7358a784363d5c47f75c691c8aff478edb23135 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exeroom536 <352890649+exeroom536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:53:04 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 25/53] Grow: clear read-auto of a member array before changing
 its size

md changes the component size of a writable array only (update_size()
returns -EROFS otherwise).  As with raid_disks, freeze() leaves read-auto
behind for a native array, but for a member of a container it freezes
the container and leaves the member array as it was, often read-auto
after assembly.  --grow --size of such a member array then fails once
the metadata handler has recorded the new size - "Cannot set device size
for ...: Read-only file system" - and Grow_reshape() rolls the metadata
back.

In Grow_reshape(), clear read-auto of a member array of external
metadata before setting its size, as the previous patch does in
reshape_array() before setting raid_disks.  A readonly set by the user
stays, and the change is refused as before.  Native arrays, and member
arrays that are writable already, go on as before.

An AMD RAIDXpert2 volume (later in this series) just assembled and grown
with --grow --size: before, the size change failed so and was rolled
back; with the change the volume grows.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model by Anthropic.
---
 Grow.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Grow.c b/Grow.c
index 0609d45c..2764a2ff 100644
--- a/Grow.c
+++ b/Grow.c
@@ -2033,6 +2033,7 @@ int Grow_reshape(char *devname, int fd,
 	/* ========= set size =============== */
 	if (s->size > 0 && (s->size == MAX_SIZE || s->size != (unsigned)array.size)) {
 		unsigned long long orig_size = get_component_size(fd) / 2;
+		char buf[SYSFS_MAX_BUF_SIZE];
 		unsigned long long min_csize;
 		struct mdinfo *mdi;
 		int raid0_takeover = 0;
@@ -2079,6 +2080,16 @@ int Grow_reshape(char *devname, int fd,
 			}
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * md changes the size of a writable array only; freeze()
+		 * clears read-auto of a native array, not of a member of a
+		 * container (as for raid_disks in reshape_array).
+		 */
+		if (st->ss->external &&
+		    sysfs_get_str(sra, NULL, "array_state", buf, sizeof(buf)) > 0 &&
+		    strncmp(buf, "read-auto", 9) == 0)
+			ioctl(fd, RESTART_ARRAY_RW, 0);
+
 		/* Update the size of each member device in case
 		 * they have been resized.  This will never reduce
 		 * below the current used-size.  The "size" attribute
